TradeLab-MCP is a research-oriented fork of PHUICMT/mcp-mt5 (MIT).

Upstream: https://github.com/PHUICMT/mcp-mt5

The original project provides the MetaTrader CLI harness (MetaEditor compile,
terminal launch, include resolution, tester.ini helpers, and parsers).

This fork adds a deterministic research layer:

- unique run_id per backtest
- exclusive run directory and tester.ini
- explicit report association (never "latest file")
- research manifest and SHA-256 provenance
- SQLite index
- MCP tools for batch, compare, and walk-forward

The official MetaTrader 5 Strategy Tester remains the only execution engine.
Python never simulates fills, spread, stops, or P&L.
